>You showed that to be true for lerpoi beginning CVV.

Those are the only lerpoi for which r,n,l are special.
All other lerpoi stand or fall independently of whether
or not they have r,n,l.

>There are still CVC and
>CCV to consider.

Anything that starts with those letters needs no special
consideration for r,n,l. The pattern is either valid or
invalid, it is also either a gismu, a lujvo or a fu'ivla,
there are no mixed patterns in this category.

>Is it possible for S1 to be a tosmabru of S3, while S4 is a
>slinku'i of S2?

S1 was the lujvo beginning with CVVRC, so it can't be a
tosmabru of anything. S2 was a corresponding fu'ivla
beginning with CVVKC, which can't be a slinku'i.

